From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] function: skip checked bodies when looking for invalid object
 literals

Every function body, the script and each module item are searched for a
CoverInitializedName (`{a=1}` left in an expression), and the search
descended into nested functions whose bodies had already been searched.
The cost grew with the nesting depth; it was about 6% of the parse
samples for reCAPTCHA's recaptcha__en.js and similar bundles.

A body parsed by FunctionStatementList is searched before it is returned
and a hit is a syntax error, so a body in the finished AST never has
one. The search now stops at function bodies. Arrow function bodies are
still searched, because a concise body (`x => expr`) is built without
that check. Parameters and class field initializers are searched as
before.

Parse time for nine third-party scripts (3.0 MiB): 254 -> 240 ms
natively. ASTs, collected source text, errors and top-level bytecode for
6009 npm files and 59 valid and invalid cover-grammar snippets are
unchanged; skipping arrow bodies too makes the snippets diverge.
